      ],
      "summary": "The desktop has Files (`@tangleai/os/files`): the person's own files in this browser, offered by a host without a server, and every application's files through a file location it serves, made from one contract template (`fileLocationContract`: paged list and search, read inline or by a signed https address, and optional write, new folder, move and delete with refusals that keep their reason). Files browses with breadcrumbs, back, forward, up and search in its header bar, previews images, PDFs and text (and Markdown or other types through the host's previewers) without ever running a file as the desktop's markup, uploads, renames, moves and deletes. The assistant reads and searches through the kernel's `tangle_os_files` and never writes a location; a location can keep the assistant out. A manifest names its location with `files`. The Pages desktop offers \"This browser\" in its own folder of the browser's private file system and draws Markdown with `@jarenjs/md`.",
      "id": "files-app"
    },
